{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083055-compiling-a-list-of-canon-dynasitic-dragon-blooded","id":1083055,"title":"Compiling a List of Canon Dynasitic Dragon-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-24T09:47:39-07:00","id":1083055,"title":"Compiling a List of Canon Dynasitic Dragon-Blooded","content":"So in anticipation of the upcoming Dragon-Blooded book. I'd decided that I want to do something I've never done before and run a Real Civil War game. I anticipate a lot of others do the same.<br /> <br /> I run my games exclusively in a Sandbox fashion, and have been playing way to many hours of Crusader Kings 2, so I thought it would be cool put together list of canon Dynasts and what we know about them. Maybe throw together some family trees etc. Realizing this is a massive undertaking, I don't actually know that much about the inner workings of the Realm, and a lot of others would likely be interested in this kind of info, I decided that I would push it out to the community and make a big project out of it.<br /> <br /> Right now this is really only the barest of ideas that I haven't thought through all that much, so lets keep it simple for now. Let's go with Character Name, Relevant Sources including page numbers, and possibly a brief description of why someone might be interested in the character.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm going to start putting together a spreadsheet, but I'm not that great at making them look nice and readable, so if someone else wants to put that together I wouldn't object<br /> <br /> Edit 2: may as well put up spreadsheet. Going is currently slow. Feel free to make changes.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1rp_SBWG1klrrsXK6vqMvSxrgsCuEWyLRz3ktoXIAIzE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1rp_SBWG1klrrsXK6vqMvSxrgsCuEWyLRz3ktoXIAIzE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1rp_SBWG1klrrsXK6vqMvSxrgsCuEWyLRz3ktoXIAIzE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1rp_SBWG1klrrsXK6vqMvSxrgsCuEWyLRz3ktoXIAIzE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","user":"Hark","date":". 04-24-2017, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:15:11-07:00","id":1083070,"title":"","content":"I remember back in the old forums, we had a thread where we put a list together of all of the canon Exalted along with the book in which they appeared, including the Dragon Blooded of course. If someone still has that list, it would make this exercise much easier, since it would just be a matter of looking on that list to see which Terrestrials were part of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:48:36-07:00","id":1083090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083055-compiling-a-list-of-canon-dynasitic-dragon-blooded?p=1083070#post1083070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember back in the old forums, we had a thread where we put a list together of all of the canon Exalted along with the book in which they appeared, including the Dragon Blooded of course. If someone still has that list, it would make this exercise much easier, since it would just be a matter of looking on that list to see which Terrestrials were part of the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Characters/ExaltedCensus\" target=\"_blank\">Something like this?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:32:03-07:00","id":1083107,"title":"","content":"Aw hell, why not?<br /> <br /> In terms of feel, the previous Devs said to read Aspect Book Air.<br /> <br /> Tepet Arada - Aspect Book Air - Aging and famous Realm General<br /> Mnemon - Aspect Book Earth - Head of House Mnemon<br /> Cathak Cainan - Aspect Book Fire - Frontrunner for the Scarlet Throne<br /> Sesus Nagezzer &quot;The Slug&quot; - Aspect Book Wood - Information broker<br /> Peleps Deled - Aspect Book Water - Shikari of the Wyld Hunt<br /> Cynis Belar Norren - Aspect Book Wood - Notable spy<br /> Tepet Ejava &quot;The Roseblack&quot; - Aspect Book Wood - Skilled General, granddaughter of Tepet Arada<br /> Ragara Bhagwei - Aspect Book Wood - Notable sorcerer, grandson of the Empress<br /> V'neef Celtis - Aspect Book Wood - Realm Folk-Hero and rogue general serving in the North<br /> Cathak Cacek Marn - Aspect Book Wood - Notable Gateway player, military leader.serving in the East, possible House of Bells instructor.<br /> V'neef Keersa Kalla - Aspect Book Wood - Notable preformer, three time widow, Lookshyan connections.<br /> Autumn Spiral - Ledaal Ansharu - Aspect Book Wood - notable Immaculate monk, tutor to Sesus Nagezzer, close friend<br /> Cynis Anbor - Aspect Book Wood - Master of Great Forks's slave and Drug Cartel, noted motherfucker, pedophile and serial killer (That suddenly went a dark place didn't it?)<br /> Peleps Japhen - Aspect Book Water - protege to Nellens Baeden<br /> Ragar Takar - Aspect Book Water - Member of the Spiral academy and the Scarlet Orchid society.<br /> Peleps Aramida - Aspect Book Water - Notable Realm naval commander<br /> Nellens Baeden - Aspect Book Water - Captain of the Grace of Daana'd, smuggler and drug trader<br /> V'neef Odessa - Aspect Book Water - Captain's Second of the Queen of Pearls, skilled diplomat and servant of house V'neef.<br /> Mnemon Tynalit Bera - Aspect Book Water - Chief Librarian of the Imperial Library<br /> Tepet Yasal - Aspect Book Water - Famous boxer, instructor at the House of Bells<br /> Peleps Danic Damanchina - Aspect Book Fire - Member of the Thousand Scales, ambitious bureaucrat<br /> Nellens Malakai - Aspect Book Fire - notable sorcerer, minor Nellens celebrity,<br /> Cynis Denovah Avaku - Aspect Book Fire - Doubting Shikari of the Wyld Hunt, notable young Legion officer<br /> Sesus Rafara - Aspect Book Fire - Assassin and master spy<br /> Sesus Taikona - Aspect Book Fire - Dedicated diplomat, brought Valis into the Realm<br /> V'neef Bijar - Aspect Book Fire - Least favorite daughter of V'neef, <br /> Sesus Chenow Lahor - Aspect Book Fire - Realm commander and rapist, stationed in the Northeast<br /> Sesus Chenow Tessani - Aspect Book Fire - Next in line for rulership of the Chenow line of house Sesus<br /> Senator Cathak Cacek Matarin - Aspect Book Fire - Aging realm senator, major player in house Cathak's political strategy<br /> Sesys Magel Kenruyo - Aspect Book Fire - Noted sorcerer-surgeon, innovator<br /> Sesus Magel Talor - Aspect Book Fire - Self-Interested uncle to Kenruyo<br /> Sesus Magel Alon - Aspect Book Fire - Self-Interested aunt to Kenruyo<br /> Cynis Takgana - Aspect Book Earth - Member of the Iron Horses, itinerant monk, member of the Immaculate Order. One-time betrothed to Peleps Dekna<br /> Peleps Dekna -Aspect Book Earth - Noted Anathema of the Solar Exalted<br /> Crow - Aspect Book Earth - Outcaste instructor at Pasiap's Stair<br /> Ragara Jasir - Aspect Book Earth - Skilled manipulator and spymaster<br /> Moias - Aspect Book Earth - Realm Magistrate<br /> Imminent Thunder - Aspect Book Earth - Ancient Immaculate Master, Wyld Hunt Shikari<br /> Dutiful Sparrow - Aspect Book Earth - Sorceress, Outcaste and demon-hunter<br /> Cynis Janism - Aspect Book Earth - Cynis reformer, Vintner<br /> Ledaal Chiska - Aspect Book Earth - Sorceress and worshipper of Autochthon<br /> Ragara Myrrun - Aspect Book Earth - Grandson of Ragara","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:36:48-07:00","id":1083111,"title":"","content":"The 3e Core rule book was significantly less helpful than expected. 2e Core has lots of interesting characters though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Added link to spread sheet in OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","user":"Hark","date":". 04-24-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T12:46:04-07:00","id":1083142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1083055-compiling-a-list-of-canon-dynasitic-dragon-blooded?p=1083090#post1083090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Characters/ExaltedCensus\" target=\"_blank\">Something like t